1 (primary), node2 and node3 (standbys), node1 writable\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"pg_basebackup seeded node2/node3 from node1 (cmd-2824b518fac34b0d, cmd-9b031869b9b34539); pg_stat_replication on node1 showed both walreceivers streaming (cmd-d1d00e9b6c1340ce, cmd-3e5bce9435b74952); a row inserted on node1 (cmd-a22aca34d9c04aa8) appeared on both standbys (cmd-e8f535e5686a4397, cmd-b22069df31544379), and node1 remained writable (pg_is_in_recovery=f, cmd-13e3deb74550437e) with standbys in recovery (pg_is_in_recovery=t, cmd-3811bf68f93c40b4/e80f46cf03424d91).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-2824b518fac34b0d\",\"cmd-9b031869b9b34539\",\"cmd-d1d00e9b6c1340ce\",\"cmd-a22aca34d9c04aa8\",\"cmd-e8f535e5686a4397\",\"cmd-b22069df31544379\",\"cmd-3811bf68f93c40b4\",\"cmd-e80f46cf03424d91\"]},{\"id\":\"tls-cluster-ca\",\"requirement\":\"Replication traffic carried over TLS using a certificate authority created for the cluster\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A dedicated CA was generated on node1 (cmd-119ef67e0a7e4409); server certs (SAN CN=nodeN) and client certs (CN=replicator) were issued and signed by that CA and verified (cmd-7c5f75705c834bdf, cmd-cca007b0c96845c4, cmd-bf682ac8c72b42a9) then distributed and installed on all nodes (cmd-7c03ddba917147c2, cmd-bf0970c506c84501, cmd-1f7f54b3b13a4167). pg_stat_ssl on node1 confirms ssl=t, a real cipher, and clientdn=/CN=replicator for both walreceiver connections, both at initial setup and after all three restarts (cmd-d1d00e9b6c1340ce, cmd-6d6c5fdbedb64df5).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-119ef67e0a7e4409\",\"cmd-7c5f75705c834bdf\",\"cmd-cca007b0c96845c4\",\"cmd-bf682ac8c72b42a9\",\"cmd-d1d00e9b6c1340ce\",\"cmd-6d6c5fdbedb64df5\"]},{\"id\":\"ca-restricted-replication\",\"requirement\":\"Accept replication connections only from peers presenting a certificate issued by the cluster CA\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"pg_hba.conf on node1 restricts replication to hostssl+cert auth from the two standby IPs only and explicitly rejects hostnossl replication from anywhere else (cmd-17f4c033f48f4343). A non-SSL replication attempt was rejected ('SSL off', cmd-5396402c476e4482), and a self-signed rogue certificate (not issued by the cluster CA) was rejected with 'SSL error: tlsv1 alert unknown ca' (cmd-6138896b89d8449f), directly demonstrating enforcement.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-17f4c033f48f4343\",\"cmd-5396402c476e4482\",\"cmd-6138896b89d8449f\"]},{\"id\":\"node1-restart-recovery\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence for node1: pre-restart baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered primary/replication state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id a9593011... captured alongside healthy streaming replication (cmd-1cdec1a71a0142c6); reboot issued (cmd-9a2d12e1db1d4ce4); mid-reboot SSH refusal observed (cmd-ef3ed7050f704542); new boot_id c3b81296... confirmed (cmd-c4362fa04c904427); node1 came back as writable primary, a post-restart write succeeded and replicated to both standbys, and TLS replication resumed (cmd-13e3deb74550437e, cmd-6d6c5fdbedb64df5, cmd-0903ed86a2894e86, cmd-75c8688cfd7a4a9f). Cross-checked against the fixed after-executor boot-identity snapshot showing the same new boot_id.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-1cdec1a71a0142c6\",\"cmd-9a2d12e1db1d4ce4\",\"cmd-ef3ed7050f704542\",\"cmd-c4362fa04c904427\",\"cmd-13e3deb74550437e\",\"cmd-6d6c5fdbedb64df5\",\"cmd-0903ed86a2894e86\",\"cmd-75c8688cfd7a4a9f\"]},{\"id\":\"node2-restart-recovery\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence for node2: pre-restart baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered standby state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 35c87ec9... captured with healthy standby state (cmd-3811bf68f93c40b4); reboot issued (cmd-9b32f56bc7a94951); mid-reboot refusal observed (cmd-bb9d76d558c74843); new boot_id 5d06dd57... confirmed (cmd-c9c67b22d73f4a91); postgresql active, in recovery, and replicated data intact post-restart (cmd-bf6b99b0a7b9485e). Cross-checked against the fixed after-executor boot-identity snapshot.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-3811bf68f93c40b4\",\"cmd-9b32f56bc7a94951\",\"cmd-bb9d76d558c74843\",\"cmd-c9c67b22d73f4a91\",\"cmd-bf6b99b0a7b9485e\"]},{\"id\":\"node3-restart-recovery\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide restart evidence for node3: pre-restart baseline, restart, changed boot identity, recovered standby state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 2f708738... captured with healthy standby state (cmd-e80f46cf03424d91); reboot issued (cmd-c247d5b6379546d4); mid-reboot refusal observed (cmd-263d53b192004c54); new boot_id 50a5d57f... confirmed (cmd-603a7794e6da4d24); postgresql active, in recovery, replicated data intact, and node1 shows node3 rejoined TLS streaming replication (cmd-76a2c3bc9cd84a3a, cmd-2331d6bdbc0546e1). Cross-checked against the fixed after-executor boot-identity snapshot.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e80f46cf03424d91\",\"cmd-c247d5b6379546d4\",\"cmd-263d53b192004c54\",\"cmd-603a7794e6da4d24\",\"cmd-76a2c3bc9cd84a3a\",\"cmd-2331d6bdbc0546e1\"]}],\"confidence\":0.92,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.8,\"summary\":\"Most state-changing commands were directly tied to installing PostgreSQL, generating/distributing the CA and certs, configuring replication, or executing the mandated restart protocol, and the executor cleaned up temporary artifacts it created (rogue cert test files removed at cmd-5588bcb31c3d46df; /tmp/tls working copy removed after the CA was archived to /etc/postgresql-tls/ca-archive with root:root 700 permissions and a 600 private key). Two mutations were made to work around a PMTU black-hole affecting node2's apt access and were left in place rather than reverted: lowering node2's ens2 interface MTU to 1400 (cmd-805c8afcc1ad4848) and rewriting node2's /etc/apt/sources.list to point at mirrors.edge.kernel.org (cmd-2f30670cae5b40f0, though a .bak backup of the original was kept). Both were bounded, low-risk, directly necessary to unblock the required package installation (a clear prerequisite for the task), and did not weaken any security control, so they are treated as minor unrestored residue rather than unnecessary mut
